pwd    — Displays the absolute path of the current working directory.
ls     — Lists files and directories in the current location.
cd     — Changes the current working directory.
mkdir  — Creates a new directory.
touch  — Creates an empty file or updates a file’s timestamp.
rm     — Deletes files or directories.
cd ..  — Moves one level up to the parent directory.
rm -rf — Forcefully and recursively deletes files or directories without confirmation.